{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"ecomseer","displayName":"EcomSeer","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/fly0pants/skills/ecomseer","publisherHandle":"fly0pants","publisherDisplayName":"fly0pants","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/fly0pants","version":"1.0.1","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1774344933269,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/ecomseer/card?ownerHandle=fly0pants&version=1.0.1","sha256":"d72846c509f0df54445e15333f6867f56dae63c64402465501746672ba9dcadb","size":2560,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"bc0fc93f4102786f7c61fe593a23a712049f336c26b60f2b99c9e5651ae18247","bundleFingerprints":["cfd0b7dcb97643afe486797fbfc4d6442ab61584eb90458044c8d552ac9e2803","24aa81ac8ef98a13a944a87544834846b29d2a79d99f7f368981ec7d2e283c5c"],"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3867,"sha256":"f6446668d0e6ab917dbe273722d1efa3832c1e624fe31ca7b11973e4f85fef7d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README_CN.md","size":3552,"sha256":"14f73e595a6ee5bc3fd6747e94d88a78417bfc4ee82b3dee74be497b96769f99","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":17833,"sha256":"6617fcdb13431dd8f397d904ccf246587a7b4f634c4078afa881fdcff37738a4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-goods.md","size":5293,"sha256":"b1b1fcb974e062ae1c004e60a8680b9ded88d6d7886fff7f76213b828e4265cd","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-shop.md","size":2903,"sha256":"46021e066d1978bab2d9725a67c36ce4545d68cb6ebfa1fa05af2b55f51bcaf6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-product-detail.md","size":3446,"sha256":"ba38dafc624e0fce33820f86e734873c6452919aae96919eb8c56af7e255ce77","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-video.md","size":3776,"sha256":"506d51c7080aa721ad5f800ca4f9f86e4da7e8565ff95ac610054c8da82a4c9d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-influencer.md","size":10761,"sha256":"ed68d269f42dd7929a23349ed9914158628239d2c39bddef47df8916d16b5266","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/api-ad.md","size":6504,"sha256":"92bddaf178726dfbd0529e840c7b47f84f18423737d50647a1e81bb329b08df8","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent EcomSeer analytics assistant, but it needs review because it stores pasted API keys and sends credentials, queries, and hosted reports through additional services without clear user control.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789434365630,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"other","level":"error","message":{"text":"API Credential and User Context Forwarded to a Secondary Service"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":136,"endLine":149}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"70a610ea04f1c6bd"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md:136-149`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Sensitive data disclosure to a secondary network service  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Complete Code Snippet\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://deepresearch.ecomseer.com/research\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer test-local-token-2026\" \\\n  -d '{\"project\": \"ecomseer\", \"query\": \"{user_query}\", \"context\": \"{additional_context}\", \"api_key\": \"'\"$ECOMSEER_API_KEY\"'\"}'\n```\n\nThe surrounding instructions explicitly require:\n\n```text\n- `query` is the user's research question (in the user's language).\n- `context` is optional — add useful context if relevant. Omit or set to `null` if not needed.\n- `api_key` passes the user's API key to the framework — always include it as shown above.\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe Skill sends the reusable `ECOMSEER_API_KEY`, the user's complete research query, and optional conversation context to `deepresearch.ecomseer.com`. This is a separate host from the primary API endpoint, `www.ecomseer.com`.\n\nSending a credential to the service against which it is directly used may be necessary for ordinary API access. Forwarding that same reusable credential to another service exceeds minimum privilege when the operation could instead use scoped delegation or locally retrieved, minimized data. The README discloses server-side deep research and hosted reports, but the reviewed instructions do not clearly provide the user with a consent step or a specific warning that the reusable API key and contextual data will be transferred.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user submits a request classified as complex, comparative, analytical, or requiring two or more API calls.\n2. The Skill automatically selects the Deep Research path.\n3. The agent validates the key against the primary API.\n4. The agent sends the reusable API key, user query, and optional context to `deepresearch.ecomseer.com`.\n5. The secondary service can receive and process the credential and potentially sensitive research content.\n6. If that service, its logging infrastructure, or an operator is compromised or untrusted, the credential can be reused against the EcomSeer API.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nExposure of the API key can grant access to whatever data, account quota, billing capacity, and API operations are authorized for that key. It can result in unauthorized API requests, credit consumption, data access, and account-level abuse within the key's scope.\n\nThe query and context may also contain confidential commercial plans, product research, identifiers, or other user-provided information. The impact extends to the secondary service and any systems used for request logging, processing, and report hosting.\n]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Do not forward the primary `ECOMSEER_API_KEY` to the Deep Research service.\n2. Perform required EcomSeer API requests in the trusted local integration and send only the minimum necessary results to the research service.\n3. If server-side access is unavoidable, exchange the primary key for a short-lived delegated token that is:\n   - Restricted to the Deep Research audience.\n   - Limited to required read-only endpoints.\n   - Bound to one task and user.\n   - Protected by a short expiration period and replay controls.\n4. Require explicit user consent before transmitting queries or conversation context to a secondary processor.\n5. Minimize and redact contextual data before transmission.\n6. Document the receiving domains, data retention period, logging policy, subprocessors, and report-sharing behavior.\n7. Provide key revocation, rotation, and task-deletion controls.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"Shell Command Injection Through Direct Substitution of Chat-Controlled Values"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":77,"endLine":83}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"6f55630e1f07cdc8"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md:77-83` and `SKILL.md:136-149`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Shell command injection and unsafe JSON construction  \n**Risk Level**: Critical\n\n### Complete Code Snippet\n\nThe Skill instructs the agent to place a key pasted into chat directly into a shell command:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw config set skills.entries.ecomseer.apiKey \"{KEY}\"\n```\n\nIt also places user-controlled query and context values directly into a shell command containing manually constructed JSON:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://deepresearch.ecomseer.com/research\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer test-local-token-2026\" \\\n  -d '{\"project\": \"ecomseer\", \"query\": \"{user_query}\", \"context\": \"{additional_context}\", \"api_key\": \"'\"$ECOMSEER_API_KEY\"'\"}'\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\n`{KEY}`, `{user_query}`, and `{additional_context}` originate from chat input. The instructions require literal replacement but do not require strict validation, shell-safe argument passing, or JSON serialization.\n\nIf an agent implements these instructions through textual shell-command construction, quotation marks, command substitutions, shell operators, newlines, or other metacharacters in an attacker-controlled value can escape the intended argument. The Deep Research command is additionally vulnerable to malformed or manipulated JSON because query and context values are inserted without JSON escaping.\n\nThe API-key configuration path is particularly dangerous because the value is embedded inside double quotes. Shell substitutions remain active inside double quotes unless the value is passed as data rather than incorporated into command source.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker sends a value that appears to be an API key or submits a research query containing shell syntax.\n2. The Skill directs the agent to replace the corresponding placeholder in the documented shell command.\n3. The agent constructs a command string rather than passing the value through a non-shell argument interface.\n4. The shell interprets injected metacharacters or substitutions.\n5. Attacker-selected commands execute with the privileges of the local OpenClaw process.\n\nAlternatively, crafted quotes and JSON syntax can alter the request body, inject additional JSON fields, or cause requests to fail in attacker-controlled ways.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful shell injection can provide arbitrary command execution under the account running OpenClaw. Depending on that account's permissions, an attacker may read or modify local files, access environment variables and configured credentials, alter Skill configuration, invoke network tools, or compromise other data available to the agent.\n\nNo evidence establishes root execution, so the confirmed scope is the effective privilege of the OpenClaw process rather than automatic system-administrator access.\n]]>","severity":"Critical"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Never generate shell source by replacing placeholders with chat-controlled text.\n2. Use a process API that accepts an executable and an argument array without invoking a shell.\n3. Validate pasted keys against a strict allowlist and expected length before storage.\n4. Reject control characters, whitespace, quotes, shell metacharacters, and unexpected prefixes in credentials.\n5. Avoid accepting credentials through chat where possible; use a protected secret-entry interface.\n6. Construct JSON with a real serializer. For shell-based implementations, use an approach such as:\n\n```bash\npayload=$(jq -n \\\n  --arg project \"ecomseer\" \\\n  --arg query \"$USER_QUERY\" \\\n  --arg context \"$ADDITIONAL_CONTEXT\" \\\n  --arg api_key \"$ECOMSEER_API_KEY\" \\\n  '{project: $project, query: $query, context: $context, api_key: $api_key}')\n```\n\n7. Pass the serialized payload as a single argument and ensure logs do not record it.\n8. Add tests containing quotes, newlines, substitutions, separators, Unicode control characters, and malformed JSON.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"Hardcoded Shared Bearer Token Embedded in Public Skill Instructions"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":140,"endLine":143}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"1ae18271e7220105"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md:140-143` and `SKILL.md:160-162`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Hardcoded authentication secret  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Complete Code Snippet\n\nThe submission request embeds a static bearer token:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://deepresearch.ecomseer.com/research\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer test-local-token-2026\" \\\n  -d '{\"project\": \"ecomseer\", \"query\": \"{user_query}\", \"context\": \"{additional_context}\", \"api_key\": \"'\"$ECOMSEER_API_KEY\"'\"}'\n```\n\nThe same token is reused for polling:\n\n```bash\nwhile true; do r=$(curl -s \"https://deepresearch.ecomseer.com/research/{task_id}\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer test-local-token-2026\"); s=$(echo \"$r\" | grep -o '\"status\":\"[^\"]*\"' | head -1 | cut -d'\"' -f4); echo \"status=$s\"; if [ \"$s\" = \"completed\" ] || [ \"$s\" = \"failed\" ]; then echo \"$r\"; break; fi; sleep 15; done\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe bearer token is stored directly in a distributed Markdown file. Anyone who obtains the Skill package can extract and replay it without needing to compromise a runtime host.\n\nA static shared bearer credential lacks per-user identity, task scoping, reliable revocation boundaries, and short-lived authorization. Its name also suggests that a test or local credential may have been deployed in production-facing instructions.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker downloads or reads the Skill.\n2. The attacker extracts `test-local-token-2026`.\n3. The attacker sends direct requests to the Deep Research submission or polling endpoints with the copied token.\n4. The service treats the attacker as an authorized bearer if the token remains active.\n5. The attacker may submit tasks, consume service resources, or interact with task results according to the permissions granted to that shared token.\n\nAccess to another user's report through polling additionally depends on whether the server properly binds task identifiers to users. The static client token provides no visible per-user separation.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe exposed token can grant all privileges assigned to the shared Deep Research credential. Potential consequences include unauthorized research submissions, resource or quota consumption, operational abuse, and access to task metadata or results if server-side task authorization is insufficient.\n\nBecause the repository does not define server-side authorization policy, broader access to arbitrary tasks cannot be conclusively established from the reviewed files alone.\n]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Revoke and rotate the exposed bearer token immediately.\n2. Remove all authentication secrets from Skill files, documentation, examples, and version history.\n3. Issue short-lived, per-user or per-installation tokens through an authenticated server-side exchange.\n4. Scope tokens to the minimum required operations and bind them to a specific task where possible.\n5. Enforce server-side ownership checks for every task submission, status request, and report retrieval.\n6. Store runtime secrets in a protected secret manager rather than source-controlled files.\n7. Add secret scanning to CI and release workflows.\n8. Monitor for historical use of the exposed credential and rate-limit abusive submission patterns.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"other","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unbounded Polling Loop Can Indefinitely Consume Agent Resources"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":158,"endLine":172}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"94141a4eae4cd3fe"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md:158-172`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unbounded network polling and availability exhaustion  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Complete Code Snippet\n\n```bash\nwhile true; do r=$(curl -s \"https://deepresearch.ecomseer.com/research/{task_id}\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer test-local-token-2026\"); s=$(echo \"$r\" | grep -o '\"status\":\"[^\"]*\"' | head -1 | cut -d'\"' -f4); echo \"status=$s\"; if [ \"$s\" = \"completed\" ] || [ \"$s\" = \"failed\" ]; then echo \"$r\"; break; fi; sleep 15; done\n```\n\nThe Skill reinforces the unbounded behavior:\n\n```text\nThis script polls every 15 seconds and exits only when the task is done. It may take 1-5 minutes. Do NOT interrupt it, do NOT add a loop limit, do NOT abandon it.\n\n- NEVER fall back to manual analysis. The framework WILL complete — just wait for it.\n- NEVER write your own polling loop. Use the exact script above.\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe loop has no maximum execution time, retry count, connection timeout, failure threshold, cancellation mechanism, or handling for malformed responses. If the service remains reachable but never returns `completed` or `failed`, the loop runs indefinitely.\n\nBecause `curl -s` suppresses diagnostics and the status parser accepts only two exact terminal values, HTTP errors, authentication failures, changed response formats, empty responses, and unexpected status values can all result in continued polling.\n\nThe accompanying instructions explicitly prohibit interrupting or bounding the loop, increasing the likelihood of resource exhaustion.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A Deep Research task is submitted.\n2. The service returns a task identifier but never returns a recognized terminal status, whether due to outage, server defect, malformed responses, or malicious behavior.\n3. The polling loop sends a request every 15 seconds indefinitely.\n4. The agent session remains occupied and continues consuming execution time and network resources.\n5. Repeated or concurrent tasks can amplify the availability impact.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe primary impact is denial of service or degraded availability of the agent process. The loop can consume session capacity, network requests, execution slots, and potentially billed runtime.\n\nThis behavior does not directly grant elevated system privileges, but it allows a remote service or persistent error condition to control how long the local agent remains occupied.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Add a fixed maximum duration and retry count.\n2. Set explicit connection and request timeouts on every HTTP request.\n3. Use exponential backoff with jitter rather than a constant interval.\n4. Stop on HTTP authentication errors, repeated server errors, malformed JSON, missing status fields, or unknown terminal states.\n5. Parse JSON with a dedicated parser instead of `grep` and `cut`.\n6. Provide a cancellation mechanism and allow the agent or user to stop the task.\n7. Return a resumable task identifier when the time budget is exceeded.\n8. Apply concurrency limits to prevent multiple polling loops from exhausting the runtime.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Package Execution Through npx Installation Command"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"README.md"},"region":{"startLine":18,"endLine":21}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"3a6afbfa3192ceff"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `README.md:18-21` and `README_CN.md:18-21`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned third-party package execution  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Complete Code Snippet\n\n```bash\nnpx clawhub install ecomseer\n```\n\nThe same installation command appears in both the English and Chinese README files.\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe installation process invokes `clawhub` through `npx` without specifying an audited version, integrity hash, lockfile, signature, or verified distribution source. Depending on the local package-manager state, `npx` can download and execute the current package version from the configured registry.\n\nThis makes the effective installer mutable after the Skill has been reviewed. A compromised publisher account, registry compromise, malicious future release, or registry configuration pointing to an untrusted source could cause different code to execute under the same documented command.\n\nThe available evidence does not establish that the current `clawhub` package is malicious. The vulnerability is the absence of dependency pinning and provenance controls.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker compromises the package publisher, registry, distribution path, or a future package release.\n2. The attacker publishes a malicious version under the package name used by the installation command.\n3. A user follows the README and runs the unpinned `npx` command.\n4. The package manager retrieves the attacker-controlled release.\n5. Package or lifecycle code executes with the privileges of the installing user.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA compromised installer can execute arbitrary code as the user performing installation. It may modify files, access user-readable credentials, alter OpenClaw configuration, install additional packages, or establish persistence if the user has sufficient permissions.\n\nNo evidence shows that this command executes with administrator privileges by default; the confirmed privilege boundary is the installing user's account.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Pin the installer to a reviewed immutable version, for example by specifying an exact package version.\n2. Publish and verify cryptographic integrity hashes or signed release attestations.\n3. Document the expected registry, package publisher, and release provenance.\n4. Use a lockfile or equivalent reproducible installation mechanism.\n5. Disable or carefully review package lifecycle scripts where practical.\n6. Audit new installer releases before updating the documented version.\n7. Add supply-chain monitoring for publisher changes, registry compromise, and unexpected package ownership transfers.\n8. Apply the same hardened installation instructions consistently to both README files.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":0,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789434106.7363687,"endTime":1789434302.600103}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"ecomseer","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57erb8vmczz4m2hb90wjxy7f98ee8wr-gT2Vzg/clawscan-skillspector-168654896/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-15T01:01:45.127797+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":95,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3867,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"README_CN.md","type":"markdown","lines":94,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3552,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":372,"executable":false,"size_bytes":17833,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-ad.md","type":"markdown","lines":249,"executable":false,"size_bytes":6504,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-goods.md","type":"markdown","lines":151,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5293,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-influencer.md","type":"markdown","lines":360,"executable":false,"size_bytes":10761,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-product-detail.md","type":"markdown","lines":126,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3446,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-shop.md","type":"markdown","lines":107,"executable":false,"size_bytes":2903,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/api-video.md","type":"markdown","lines":134,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3776,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-40a9d603720e4a649e739e276d5fbbbb","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":77,"end_line":83},"finding":null,"explanation":"Automatically configuring a persistently stored API key from chat input without a clear warning or explicit confirmation is unsafe secret handling. Users may unknowingly disclose credentials into logs/transcripts and may not realize the key is being stored for future use.","remediation":"Eliminate automatic persistence from chat input. Use explicit consent, dedicated secret input channels, and clear disclosure about storage scope, duration, and usage; ideally require configuration outside the conversation entirely.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":77,"end_line":83}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-9df61a1c0e764ad789eb74f6814cab12","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":77,"end_line":83},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly encourages users to paste API keys into chat and then persists those secrets in configuration, violating the principle of minimizing secret exposure. Chat channels are often logged, reviewed, or retained, so this pattern substantially raises the risk of credential leakage and unauthorized reuse.","remediation":"Do not request or process API keys through chat. Redirect users to a secure credential-management UI or environment-secret mechanism, and document that secrets should never be pasted into conversation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":77,"end_line":83}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-e89b75f1f64544dd80d943e0181a4cf2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":136,"end_line":150},"finding":null,"explanation":"The deep research workflow forwards the user's EcomSeer API key to a separate service at `deepresearch.ecomseer.com`, which is a different trust boundary than the advertised API host. Forwarding credentials to another backend enables credential reuse, mishandling, logging, or compromise outside the user's expected scope, and the manifest does not clearly justify this delegation.","remediation":"Do not transmit the user's API key to secondary services. Perform deep research using the primary service directly, or use a server-side token exchange where the skill backend calls EcomSeer on the user's behalf without exposing the user's credential to another domain; clearly disclose any subprocessor/service involvement in the manifest and consent flow.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":136,"end_line":150}]},{"id":"P6","finding_id":"finding-1431a1ef783641c6aa60f56adfea1a7a","category":"System Prompt Leakage","pattern":"Direct Prompt Extraction","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":351,"end_line":null},"finding":"Output Guidelines","explanation":"Skill contains instructions that could directly expose system prompts, internal rules, or hidden instructions to users or external parties.","remediation":"Remove any instructions that reveal, print, or output system prompts or internal rules. System instructions should never be exposed to end users.","code_snippet":"\n**Reuse data:** If the user asks follow-up questions about already-fetched data, analyze existing results first. Only make new API calls when needed.\n\n## Output Guidelines\n\n1. **Language consistency** — ALL output must match the user's detected language.\n2. **Route-appropriate output** — Don't dump tables for browsing; don't skip data for analysis.","intent":null,"tags":["System Prompt Leakage","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"83cf929697970eb90cc7127b9caf72ca04cca2a98055f845c38d7cab79be2614","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":351,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-91b66d0a1f4e489faa9b943491b99ae3","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":21,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README instructs users to run `npx clawhub install ecomseer` without pinning a specific version. This creates a supply-chain risk because the latest published package version will be executed at install time, and a compromised or malicious update could run arbitrary code on the user's machine. In the context of an install command in documentation, this is a real security issue even if likely unintentional.","remediation":"Pin the exact package version in the install command, for example `npx clawhub@<version> install ecomseer`, and document upgrade procedures separately. Consider providing checksum/signature verification guidance and linking to a trusted release page so users can validate what they are installing.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7262d2d74474470a7918d81d46269adc58e41b14f04615fa861813226ce136df","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":21,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-334c61e7a9dd4cf185af27a7a432ad0b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":70,"end_line":87},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README states that Deep Research reports are 'hosted and shareable via link' but does not prominently warn users about the privacy and confidentiality implications. Generated reports may contain sensitive market research, shop comparisons, influencer analysis, or proprietary business strategy, and hosting them by default can expose that information through unintended sharing or discoverability. Given this skill's focus on commercial intelligence, the context increases the sensitivity of the hosted output.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that Deep Research outputs are hosted remotely and may contain sensitive business data. Make report hosting/shareability opt-in by default, document access controls and retention policies, and provide a private/local-only or non-shareable report option where possible.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":70,"end_line":87}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-7431ea44935242d1a2de4d3abf7c675a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":72,"end_line":78},"finding":null,"explanation":"The Deep Research activation criteria are described very broadly, including automatic triggering for queries requiring '2+ API calls or cross-entity reasoning.' This ambiguity can cause users to invoke a more expansive server-side processing mode than expected, increasing the chance that more data, context, or sensitive business queries are sent to hosted infrastructure without explicit, informed consent. In a data-intelligence skill handling commercial analysis, implicit escalation to deeper processing is more dangerous because users may assume they are doing simple lookups.","remediation":"Define precise, user-visible activation rules for Deep Research and require explicit opt-in before switching from normal lookups to server-side research mode. Add documentation describing what data is sent, how long processing takes, what outputs are produced, and how users can disable or confirm this mode per request.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":72,"end_line":78}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-26d05169ccf44fe2b00ae7f385b38ec6","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"README_CN.md","start_line":21,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The installation command uses `npx clawhub` without pinning a specific version, so users may execute whatever package version is current at install time. This creates a supply-chain risk: a compromised upstream release or typosquatted dependency could run attacker-controlled code on the user's machine during installation.","remediation":"Pin the exact package and preferably its integrity/source, for example by documenting a fixed version such as `npx clawhub@<version> install ecomseer`. Also provide verification guidance, such as checking publisher identity, release provenance, or using a lockfile-based/package-manager installation path instead of an unpinned one-off execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7262d2d74474470a7918d81d46269adc58e41b14f04615fa861813226ce136df","occurrences":[{"file":"README_CN.md","start_line":21,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-ab58faf3d73e46eb8c2539a755c45a26","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"README_CN.md","start_line":69,"end_line":77},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README states that 'deep research' is automatically triggered for broad classes of queries, including any request requiring more than two API calls or cross-entity reasoning. Such vague activation criteria can cause users to unintentionally invoke a more powerful server-side workflow, increasing the chance of unexpected data processing, higher-cost actions, or transmission of sensitive business queries beyond what the user intended.","remediation":"Narrow and explicitly define the trigger conditions for deep research, and require explicit user confirmation before activating server-side multi-step analysis. Document clear examples of what will be sent, what processing occurs, expected cost/latency, and provide a way to disable automatic escalation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README_CN.md","start_line":69,"end_line":77}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0739baf70980424988df15fe37db1e5f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"README_CN.md","start_line":69,"end_line":86},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document says the feature uses a server-side AI research system and produces hosted, shareable online HTML reports, but it does not clearly warn users that their queries and possibly derived analysis data are sent off-platform and stored in a shareable form. In an e-commerce intelligence context, user prompts may contain sensitive market research, shop strategy, product plans, or competitor analysis, so undisclosed remote processing and link-based sharing materially increases confidentiality risk.","remediation":"Add a prominent privacy/security notice before describing deep research. Clearly state that prompts and related data are transmitted to EcomSeer's servers, explain retention/storage/sharing behavior for hosted reports, default reports to private/unshared access, and require explicit opt-in before creating shareable links. Provide data handling, deletion, and access-control details.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README_CN.md","start_line":69,"end_line":86}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-756afce7f460424686bab8b1eaad2f65","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest description lists generic English triggers such as \"find trending,\" \"shop data,\" \"product research,\" and \"e-commerce analytics,\" along with short Chinese phrases like \"带货\" and \"爆品.\" These are broad topical terms rather than narrowly scoped invocation phrases, which increases the chance of unintended activation during normal conversation about e-commerce.","remediation":"Restrict triggers to explicit, skill-specific phrases or command-style invocations, and add scope constraints or negative examples. For example, use phrases like \"use EcomSeer to search TikTok Shop products\" instead of broad category terms.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-e36c663f7afa4d0cac2244958dc05ea7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":77,"end_line":83},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs the agent to accept an API key pasted into chat and persist it into local configuration, expanding from data assistance into credential handling. This creates unnecessary secret exposure risk in chat history and local state, and can surprise users because persistence occurs automatically without explicit consent or secure input handling.","remediation":"Remove the chat-based key intake and automatic `openclaw config set` flow. Require users to configure `ECOMSEER_API_KEY` through the platform's dedicated secret-management mechanism, and if key setup guidance is needed, provide instructions that direct users to secure settings rather than pasting secrets into conversation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":77,"end_line":83}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-aac6c74cfc4c4576823bfc0199796af9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":119,"end_line":194},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes analytics via `ecomseer.com`, but the implementation additionally relies on `deepresearch.ecomseer.com` and publishes reports on `r2.dev`, which materially changes the data-flow and hosting surface. This mismatch undermines informed consent and security review because user data and outputs may be sent to or hosted by services not declared in the skill description.","remediation":"Update the manifest and user-facing documentation to accurately disclose all external domains, data recipients, and report-hosting locations. Prefer minimizing third-party/external hosts, and keep all processing/report delivery under the declared domain when possible.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":119,"end_line":194}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-dc8cee9cf1be4dfcb528b301b702206c","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":127,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" \"https://www.ecomseer.com/api/open/goods/filters?region=US\" -H \"X-API-Key: $ECOMSEER_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n- If it returns `200` → key is valid, proceed to Step 1.\n- If ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\nRun this command first to verify the API key is valid:\n```bash\ncurl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" \"https://www.ecomseer.com/api/open/goods/filters?region=US\" -H \"X-API-Key: $ECOMSEER_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n- If it returns `200` → key is valid, proceed to Step 1.","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b14551118841fdda19234883b4b934f49bf30877a6d9e62094b2064910f6e4b9","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":127,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-489bfb718a5549a49ec5165047184112","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/api-goods.md","start_line":1,"end_line":151},"finding":null,"explanation":"The entire skill documentation is written only in Chinese, with no indication that users may choose another language or that the skill is intended exclusively for a Chinese-speaking or region-specific audience. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in can be a natural-language policy violation.","remediation":"Add a note that the skill supports multiple languages or is intended specifically for Chinese-speaking users, or provide an English/localized version so language choice is explicit and documented.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-goods.md","start_line":1,"end_line":151}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bf2b457deb954d16a9659dc97a12b154","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/api-influencer.md","start_line":131,"end_line":135},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation explicitly exposes an influencer contact-information subinterface and states that contact details may be returned, but it provides no privacy warning, access-control requirements, consent basis, or data-handling limitations. In an e-commerce intelligence skill, this increases the risk of harvesting personal contact data for unsolicited outreach, spam, or broader privacy misuse.","remediation":"Add explicit privacy and acceptable-use guidance stating what contact fields may be returned, the lawful basis/consent requirements for accessing them, and restrictions on storage, export, and outreach. Require authorization checks for contact endpoints, minimize returned PII by default, redact sensitive fields unless the caller has a justified permission scope, and document retention/audit requirements.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-influencer.md","start_line":131,"end_line":135}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-17633f4eb9d24bea97f353ef0553e64f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/api-ad.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown repeatedly sets `region` default values to `US`, which imposes a locale/market default in the skill documentation rather than presenting a user choice or documenting why the US locale is required. Under the policy, forcing a specific locale without opt-in can be a natural-language policy concern when no justification is given.","remediation":"Document that the user may choose the target market explicitly, or explain why `US` is the required default for this skill. If US is only an example, label it as an example rather than a fixed default.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-ad.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-ea0df36f37504481b92f792e8894650f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.77,"location":{"file":"references/api-influencer.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation repeatedly sets `region` default values to `US`, establishing a locale-specific default behavior. Because no user choice, opt-in, or justification is provided in the natural-language description, this can be read as a locale policy issue under the language/locale policy rule.","remediation":"Document why `US` is the default region, or explicitly prompt users to choose a region/market before using the endpoints. If the API is primarily US-focused, state that limitation clearly in the description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-influencer.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-b4464e33e4724a049be50b4defd1a55c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/api-product-detail.md","start_line":1,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file presents the skill/API documentation in Chinese by default, and there is no indication that users can choose another language or have opted into Chinese-only content. The policy explicitly calls for flagging language or locale constraints when a specific language is forced without user opt-in.","remediation":"Provide a language option, add an English version, or clearly state that this documentation is intended for a specific Chinese-language audience with justification.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-product-detail.md","start_line":1,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-2503af523b724e44b593a96335939df5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/api-shop.md","start_line":1,"end_line":107},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file presents the skill documentation entirely in Chinese, including headings, parameter descriptions, and cautions, without indicating that users may choose another language or that the locale restriction is required for a region-specific purpose. Under the language/locale policy check, this is a natural-language policy concern because it imposes a specific language without opt-in.","remediation":"Add a language choice or note that the documentation is available in multiple languages, or explicitly justify that the skill is intended only for a Chinese-speaking audience or region-specific workflow.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-shop.md","start_line":1,"end_line":107}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-9f38e3fc9ece47689daf2d51d9e0bcb6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/api-video.md","start_line":21,"end_line":21},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown repeatedly specifies `region` with a default value of `US`, which imposes a locale/market default in the skill documentation. Under the policy, forcing a specific locale without user opt-in or clear justification can be a natural-language policy violation.","remediation":"Document that the user may choose the target region explicitly, or explain why `US` is the required default for this skill. If multiple regions are supported, present `US` as an example rather than a fixed default.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-video.md","start_line":21,"end_line":21}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-6dd0327cffec421f9679b7da32065ad9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/api-video.md","start_line":50,"end_line":50},"finding":null,"explanation":"This line defines `region` with a default of `US`, again creating a locale preference in the natural-language/API description. Because the file does not explain why US is mandatory or invite user selection, it may conflict with the language/locale policy guidance.","remediation":"Allow or encourage explicit region selection in the documentation, or add a brief justification for the US default if the endpoint is intentionally region-specific.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-video.md","start_line":50,"end_line":50}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-de67735f3b3d4904a7968a731cc53274","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/api-video.md","start_line":69,"end_line":69},"finding":null,"explanation":"The parameter table hard-codes `US` as the default target market, which is a locale choice expressed in natural language. The file does not state that this is optional user-configurable behavior or that the endpoint is limited to that locale for compliance or product reasons.","remediation":"State that users should supply their desired region where applicable, or justify the default region clearly in the documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-video.md","start_line":69,"end_line":69}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-b3d04c1f44da47d49ddb93627979a25b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/api-video.md","start_line":98,"end_line":98},"finding":null,"explanation":"Using `US` as the default `region` sets a locale preference in the documented behavior. The policy allows this only when the user is given a choice or when the locale restriction is clearly justified, neither of which is present here.","remediation":"Revise the docs to indicate region selection is user-controlled, or add clear justification if the endpoint is intended for US-only use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/api-video.md","start_line":98,"end_line":98}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-659700bf4ea7443b9cfe28dcad741f42","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/api-video.md","start_line":117,"end_line":117},"finding":null,"explanation":"This repeats the same locale defaulting pattern by setting `region` to `US` in the parameter table. Because the documentation does not present this as an opt-in or explain a US-only constraint, it may violate the locale policy criterion.","remediation":"Make re